# The build context is the repository root, because the image is built from this
# module's own go.mod. BuildKit reads the ignore file named after the Dockerfile
# when one exists, which is what keeps this scoped to the lab instead of adding a
# .dockerignore at the root that every other build in the repo would inherit.
#
# .git is the whole of the point: it is larger than the source and no build step
# reads it.
.git
.github
.claude
docs
examples
